I'd actually patched my own local version to display the weights of
items (Vulture-style in arbitrary units, by appending (w:40) or
whatever to the item description). I chose to show weights of all
items that were in inventory, or on the ground and where the character
could plausibly pick them up to determine their weight (this includes
everything but trice corpses and gray stones, which the character
couldn't feel the weight of without the risk of being unable to drop
them again). The only other thing you need to change to avoid spoiling
a lot of information is the weight of gauntlets of power, as far as I
can tell (they're the only gloves with the weight they have), although
some other random-appearance group of items (IIRC boots?) don't have
consistent weights within an appearance group, and so that leaks some
information compared to vanilla too.

